  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Ephesians",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 5,
    "summary": "The Saints are exhorted to avoid uncleanness and walk uprightly—Husbands and wives should love each other.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Be ye therefore followers of God, as dear children;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "GR imitators. 1 Cor. 11:1; Philip. 3:17 (13–21). TG God, the Standard of Righteousness; Jesus Christ, Exemplar."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And walk in love, as Christ also hath loved us, and hath given himself for us an offering and a sacrifice to God for a sweetsmelling savour.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Walking with God."
          },
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 89,
            "text": "Heb. 8:3."
          },
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 105,
            "text": "TG Self-Sacrifice."
          },
          {
            "start": 133,
            "end": 139,
            "text": "Gen. 8:21; Lev. 1:9."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But fornication, and all uncleanness, or covetousness, let it not be once named among you, as becometh saints;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "TG Chastity; Fornication; Sexual Immorality."
          },
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 109,
            "text": "TG Saints."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Neither filthiness, nor foolish talking, nor jesting, which are not convenient: but rather giving of thanks.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "TG Filthiness."
          },
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "TG Levity."
          },
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 39,
            "text": "Eccl. 5:2; Matt. 12:36."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For this ye know, that no whoremonger, nor unclean person, nor covetous man, who is an idolater, hath any inheritance in the kingdom of Christ and of God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "TG Chastity; Whore."
          },
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "TG Uncleanness."
          },
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 117,
            "text": "TG Inheritance; Worthiness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let no man deceive you with vain words: for because of these things cometh the wrath of God upon the children of disobedience.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "TG Deceit."
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 84,
            "text": "TG God, Indignation of."
          },
          {
            "start": 113,
            "end": 125,
            "text": "TG Disobedience."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Be not ye therefore partakers with them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For ye were sometimes darkness, but now are ye light in the Lord: walk as children of light:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "TG Children of Light."
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "Rom. 12:2."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 46
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "(For the fruit of the Spirit is in all goodness and righteousness and truth;)",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "TG Good Works."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 31
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Proving what is acceptable unto the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And have no fellowship with the unfruitful works of darkness, but rather reprove them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "Gen. 49:6; Ps. 1:1 (1–2); Prov. 1:10 (10–19)."
          },
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "TG Darkness, Spiritual."
          },
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 80,
            "text": "TG Reproof."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 86
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For it is a shame even to speak of those things which are done of them in secret.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "TG Shame."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But all things that are reproved are made manifest by the light: for whatsoever doth make manifest is light.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore he saith, Awake thou that sleepest, and arise from the dead, and Christ shall give thee light.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 98,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Light of the World; Light [noun]."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "See then that ye walk circumspectly, not as fools, but as wise,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Redeeming the time, because the days are evil.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore be ye not unwise, but understanding what the will of the Lord is.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "TG Wisdom."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 75
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And be not drunk with wine, wherein is excess; but be filled with the Spirit;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Drunkenness; Word of Wisdom."
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "TG Temperance."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Speaking to yourselves in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, singing and making melody in your heart to the Lord;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "TG Singing."
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 89,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 3:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Giving thanks always for all things unto God and the Father in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "TG Thanksgiving."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Submitting yourselves one to another in the fear of God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "TG Reconciliation."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wives, submit yourselves unto your own husbands, as unto the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Continuing Courtship in."
          },
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "Esth. 1:20 (20–22). TG Submissiveness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the husband is the head of the wife, even as Christ is the head of the church: and he is the saviour of the body.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Husbands."
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Head of the Church."
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 81,
            "text": "TG Church."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore as the church is subject unto Christ, so let the wives be to their own husbands in every thing.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 54
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Husbands, love your wives, even as Christ also loved the church, and gave himself for it;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Family, Patriarchal."
          },
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "TG Family, Love within; Love."
          },
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Continuing Courtship in."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "That he might sanctify and cleanse it with the washing of water by the word,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "TG Sanctification."
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "TG Purification."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "That he might present it to himself a glorious church, not having spot, or wrinkle, or any such thing; but that it should be holy and without blemish.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "So ought men to love their wives as their own bodies. He that loveth his wife loveth himself.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Wives."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For no man ever yet hated his own flesh; but nourisheth and cherisheth it, even as the Lord the church:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "TG Hate."
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 39,
            "text": "TG Body, Sanctity of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For we are members of his body, of his flesh, and of his bones.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "1 Cor. 6:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For this cause shall a man leave his father and mother, and shall be joined unto his wife, and they two shall be one flesh.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 113,
            "end": 116,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Celestial; Unity."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "This is a great mystery: but I speak concerning Christ and the church.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "TG Mysteries of Godliness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Nevertheless let every one of you in particular so love his wife even as himself; and the wife see that she reverence her husband.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 94,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Wives."
          },
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 117,
            "text": "TG Courtesy; Respect."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 95,
            "end": 98
          },
          {
            "start": 118,
            "end": 121
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
